Found 2026-08-30 via `openplanet-lsp check` on tm-dips-plus-plus. Two error strings, one defect. The typedb already has `Text::Format(const string&in, uint)` and `Text::Format(const string&in, float)` — this is not a missing overload.

## Steps to Reproduce

`openplanet-lsp check` on tm-dips-plus-plus (or the one-file plugin below).

Live errors:

```
src/DebugWindow.as:265:78: error: No matching signatures to 'Text::Format(const string, uint)'
src/DebugWindow.as:269:85: error: No matching signatures to 'Text::Format(const string, uint)'
src/DebugWindow.as:270:85: error: No matching signatures to 'Text::Format(const string, uint)'
src/MainUI/Donations.as:24:99: error: No matching signatures to 'Text::Format(const string, float)'
```

Minimal (verified 2026-08-30 against the live binary):

```angelscript
uint get_Off() { return 1; }
const uint16 SZ = 4;

class C {
    float last = 1.5;
    float get_Amt() { return last; }
}

void Use() {
    uint u = 3;
    float f = 1.5;
    C@ c = C();
    Text::Format("0x%04x", u);   // silent
    Text::Format("%.2f", f);     // silent
    Text::Format("0x%04x", SZ);  // silent
    Text::Format("0x%04x", Off);     // ERR: Text::Format(const string, uint)
    Text::Format(" ($%.2f)", c.Amt); // ERR: Text::Format(const string, float)
}
```

## Expected Behavior

Silent on all five calls. A virtual property (`get_X` / `get_Amt`) used as a value is a value. The game compiles the dips++ call sites.

## Actual Behavior

Only the getter forms error. Locals of the same primitive type, and a `const uint16`, are accepted. So the uint/float overloads resolve; the getter expression does not bind as a value.

## Why

B023's `arg_is_function_shaped` asks `lookup_arg_function_sigs`, which calls `lookup_function_overloads`. That helper's `workspace_function_property_candidates` also tries `get_{name}` / `set_{name}`.

So:

- bare ident `Off` finds free function `get_Off` → function-shaped
- member `c.Amt` finds method `C::get_Amt` via `lookup_method_overloads_with_inheritance` → `lookup_function_overloads("C::Amt")` → `C::get_Amt` → function-shaped

A function-shaped arg into a non-funcdef parameter rejects every candidate (`check_external_overload_set`). `Text::Format`'s second param is `uint`/`float`/etc., never a funcdef, so the whole set dies and the diagnostic renders the getter's *return* type (`uint` / `float`).

That is why the message looks like a missing `Text::Format` overload. It is not.

`const uint16 SZ` is a variable, not a getter, so it never takes this path — which is why DebugWindow.as:266-268 (`SZ_*` / `LEN_*` uint16 consts) are silent next to :265/:269/:270 (uint getters).

## Live call sites (game accepts)

- tm-dips-plus-plus `src/DebugWindow.as:265,269,270` — `Text::Format("0x%04x", O_CSmPlayer_NetPacketsBuf)` and the other two `uint get_O_*` properties in `src/Dev.as`
- tm-dips-plus-plus `src/MainUI/Donations.as:24` — `Text::Format(" ($%.2f)", cheers[i].TotalAmt)` where `float get_TotalAmt()` lives on `Donations::DonoCheerCount`

## Work

`arg_is_function_shaped` / `lookup_arg_function_sigs` must not treat a virtual-property *value* use as a function. `get_X` is a function when written `get_X` or `&get_X`; `X` is a value.

Do not drop `get_`/`set_` from `lookup_function_overloads` wholesale — other callers (value typing, member lookup) need that. Split the candidate set, or skip `get_`/`set_` alts on the B023 function-shaped path.

Do not "fix" this by silencing `Text::Format`. Any non-funcdef parameter will false-reject a getter the same way (`Math::Max(Off, 0)`, `tostring(c.Amt)`, …). `Text::Format` is just where dips++ hits it.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)

Red: the two getter lines in the minimal plugin above.

Variants:

- free-function getter (`get_Off` / `Off`) — uint, float, int, bool, string
- class getter (`c.Amt`) — same primitives
- namespaced class getter (`Ns::C@` / `Ns::get_X`)
- local of the same type stays silent
- `const` of the same type stays silent
- actual function passed to `Text::Format` still errors (keep B023)
- `startnew(get_Off)` / real method reference still function-shaped
- `Text::Format("%d", u)` uint local still silent
- a non-Format non-funcdef call with a getter arg (`Math::Max(Off, 1)`) — same FP, same fix

Game probe the fixture before treating LSP silence as ground truth.

## Related

B023 (function-shaped args vs funcdef slots — this is that rule over-firing on virtual properties), GH #47 (`No matching signatures` render), tm-dips-plus-plus `src/DebugWindow.as` / `src/MainUI/Donations.as` / `src/Dev.as`.

## Lane decision + framing (coordinator, 2026-08-30)

**Serialised with B061 and B062 into one lane (`b060-b062-property-semantics`),
B060 first.** File overlap, not size: B060 touches `src/typecheck/checker.rs`
(`arg_is_function_shaped` / `lookup_arg_function_sigs`), B061 touches
`checker.rs` record-use paths AND `src/analysis/unused.rs`, B062 touches
`unused.rs` and `src/workspace/manifest.rs`. B060-B061 collide in `checker.rs`;
B061-B062 collide in `unused.rs`. Run in parallel they would conflict at merge
and each would review against a base the other invalidated.

**BLOCKED until B059 merges.** lane-b059 is live in `checker.rs` right now
(injected-method table, unifying both GH #21 sites). Do not open this lane
until I have merged it and told you to branch from that tip.

**Framing worth having before you start.** B060 and B061 are the same missing
concept seen from opposite sides. The codebase has no single answer to *is this
identifier a property read or a function reference?*, so each site decides for
itself and they disagree:

- **B060 applies the `X` <-> `get_X` mapping where it must not.** A property
  READ (`Off`, `c.Amt`) is classified function-SHAPED because `get_Off`
  exists, so it cannot bind to a `uint`/`float` parameter and every overload
  dies.
- **B061 fails to apply it where it must.** The same property read does not
  credit `get_Off` as used, so the accessor is reported unused.

One read, two sites, opposite wrong answers. Consider whether a single shared
predicate ("this expression is a property read, and its value type is the
getter's return type") fixes both, rather than patching each site. If it does,
say so and do it once. If it does not, say why — that is a real finding either
way and belongs in the ledger.

Do NOT let that framing widen the tickets. Each keeps its own red test and its
own gate; the shared predicate is an implementation option, not a licence to
refactor property handling wholesale.